{"id": "EUVD-2026-76570", "enisaUuid": "c9cca5a0-9cda-327c-905d-376fa111b216", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent client use-after-free during NFSv4.0 revoked-state cleanup\n\nnfs40_clean_admin_revoked() takes a stateid reference under\nclp->cl_lock, drops nn->client_lock, and calls\nnfsd4_drop_revoked_stid(), which dereferences the stateid's client\nthrough s->sc_client->cl_lock.  The stateid reference does not pin the\nclient, so a teardown racing the dropped lock can free the client\nwhile nfsd4_drop_revoked_stid() is still using it.\n\nThis cleanup runs from the laundromat, so a periodic sweep can race\nforce_expire_client() driven by a write to the clients/<id>/ctl file.\n\nSkip a client that is already expiring and otherwise pin it with\ncl_rpc_users under client_lock before dropping the lock, matching\nnfsd4_revoke_states().", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:50:29", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ae0d2b5c5a1b39c0b3c15d96b32a5b0c583d519", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b413ec5b23e3445dc9c4f273116078e2d4747626", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81cf7f1413862f87b078920c838460a6a88aa030", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7b4f8a1586c42d3afc3c0ac779af2db7ab1a5c55"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mr23-3fxm-cw86", "CVE-2026-89658"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.62, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05d0f056-afd5-38e3-8d31-a3a3cfb44553", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1c7f2f16-a2a1-359f-b27f-c507f97d2cab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d688d8585e6bea5e4e37f7497feea93b6b0a469c <0ae0d2b5c5a1b39c0b3c15d96b32a5b0c583d519"}, {"id": "25953280-5b81-3683-9d4b-12c8d64485a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "6124778a-5534-39f2-b380-ee0e9e1fd14b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d688d8585e6bea5e4e37f7497feea93b6b0a469c <7b4f8a1586c42d3afc3c0ac779af2db7ab1a5c55"}, {"id": "718ce5ae-9df5-390d-aa39-4bb454a0fd00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "99710a82-a249-32b7-905c-e17499a58780", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "a732c457-7382-35e8-9165-c7e2ee60e6e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b9b5cbab-6c11-3806-a977-033b2a70b230", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d688d8585e6bea5e4e37f7497feea93b6b0a469c <b413ec5b23e3445dc9c4f273116078e2d4747626"}, {"id": "c0586092-3338-39a4-b944-ac129f69469e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "c3edbb56-2031-3683-a365-970c0b8d76e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d688d8585e6bea5e4e37f7497feea93b6b0a469c <81cf7f1413862f87b078920c838460a6a88aa030"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "02769ab6-2a06-31ce-bf4b-f85aa89886ac", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}